# WRF Build And Run Hygiene

Use this rule for WRF build, configure, install, idealized-case, runtime-output, or artifact-staging work.

- Prefer out-of-source build/install directories such as `_build*` and `install*`; keep generated artifacts ignored.
- For quick model proof, prefer idealized cases before WPS or real-weather workflows: `em_b_wave`, `em_grav2d_x`, or `em_quarter_ss`.
- Before long builds or simulations, confirm the target case, build directory, install directory, MPI/OpenMP settings, and expected runtime.
- For smoke runs, shorten `namelist.input` in an installed or ignored test copy, not the source test case unless requested.
- Inspect NetCDF output with tools such as `ncdump`; do not try to open binary `wrfout*` files as text.
- Do not stage `wrfout*`, `wrfinput*`, `wrfbdy*`, `rsl.*`, `*.o`, `*.mod`, binaries, build directories, or installed test artifacts unless explicitly requested.
